From: Cage maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] qemu: bind Windows AF_UNIX sockets under an ASCII spelling

QEMU cannot bind a chardev socket whose path has non-ASCII characters on
Windows, as when the user name is Chinese ("Failed to bind socket ...:
network down"). QEMU sockets, their driver-side dials and the usernet
sockets now use the directory's 8.3 alias when the instance path is not
ASCII. Disk, log and other file paths keep their long spelling.

